 "headline": {
  "question": "How much does building the warehouse model cost Storm, compared with the on-the-fly pipeline?",
  "answer": "Little. Storm builds the reachable model itself, from a symbolic description, in about 3 seconds and 470 MB.",
  "storm_builds_the_671532_state_model_from_a_prism_module_in_s": 2.805,
  "storm_states_built": 671532,
  "storm_transitions_built": 3170176,
  "storm_peak_memory_mb": 470,
  "storm_total_wall_both_bounds_s": 19.16,
  "ours_bfs_s": 12.468,
  "ours_robust_vi_both_bounds_s": 104.61,
  "ours_total_s": 118.46,
  "speedup_end_to_end": 6.2,
  "writing_the_prism_module_took_s": 0.006,
  "prism_module_size_bytes": 80155,
  "prism_module_commands": 164,
  "storm_full_sigma_build_s": 34.483,
  "storm_full_sigma_states": 7952112,
  "storm_full_sigma_peak_memory_mb": 4442,
  "ours_full_sigma_materialize_s": 24.5,
  "ours_full_sigma_vi_both_bounds_s": 891.9,
  "ours_full_sigma_peak_rss_gb": 5.5,
  "verdict": "Handed a 164-command PRISM module over (x,y,stage,bat,w,chg) -- 80 kB of text that takes 6 ms to emit -- Storm performs the reachability itself, builds exactly the same 671,532 states and 3,170,176 transitions that BFS finds here, and returns both certified bounds (abs. error 2.5e-11 / 3.1e-11, at the limit of Storm's 10-digit printing) in 9.6 s wall per bound: 2.8 s build + 6.3 s model check, 470 MB. The Python pipeline (case3.build) needs 12.5 s for the BFS and 105 s for the two robust value iterations. The un-optimized encoding (4,628 per-cell commands instead of 164 rectangle-compressed ones) builds in 84 s, and building ALL 7,952,112 declared states with no reachability pruning costs Storm 34 s and 4.4 GB, against 24.5 s + 892 s of VI at 5.5 GB for the materialized-Sigma baseline of case3.py. Model construction is not the bottleneck at this scale; it is 3% of Storm's own runtime and about 2.5% of the Python pipeline's. storm-pars' *refined* parameter lifting had certified nothing after 8,961 region splits and 900 s, while its single-region relaxation, the analogue of the interval composition, costs 23 s on the pruned model and certifies a strictly narrower interval than the interval composition."
 }
